IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa9-penalties.l4: one helper that the offence sections of this part share.
-- The Act states every fine as "a fine", "a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum" or "a fine not exceeding
-- level N on the standard scale" (and a fraction of one of those). The pounds that the statutory maximum and
-- a level stand for are not in the Act, so they are INPUTS here, never numbers from memory (PLAN.md section 3).
--
-- The first fine in this part is s 414D(3)(b), so the helper carries that label.

§ `s 414D(3) the pounds a fine limit allows`

-- src:5547 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:5548 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:5549 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 414D(3) Penalty on summary conviction: a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (src:5547-5549)
GIVEN limit IS A `Fine limit`
      `the pounds the statutory maximum stands for` IS A NUMBER
      `the pounds the level of the limit stands for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 414D(3) the most a fine limit allows in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER limit
    WHEN `a fine without a stated limit` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "to a fine" states no amount
    WHEN `a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` fraction THEN JUST (fraction TIMES `the pounds the statutory maximum stands for`)
    WHEN `a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` lvl fraction THEN JUST (fraction TIMES `the pounds the level of the limit stands for`)
    WHEN `a fine not exceeding an amount in pounds` amount THEN JUST amount
